{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood","id":1143918,"title":"Vermin flood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-25T16:30:56-07:00","id":1143918,"title":"Vermin flood","content":"*Once activated, every animal of Size 2 or lower immediately swarms with the speed and intensity of the vampire\u2019s Celerity and <br /> Vigor (persistent effects only).*<br /> <br /> What does exactly means: with the speed and intensity of vampire's celerity and vigor?<br /> Why should it be different from a swarm summoned with animalism 3? Animalism 3 summons all the animals in the range as well as the description of this power do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T16:42:14-07:00","id":1143919,"title":"","content":"Vigor and celerity increase speed, so the animals will get there quicker with vermin flood than with summon the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T18:35:41-07:00","id":1143934,"title":"","content":"Doubled. Sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-25-2017, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T18:38:14-07:00","id":1143935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1143919#post1143919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vigor and celerity increase speed, so the animals will get there quicker with vermin flood than with summon the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celerity does not increase speed. <br /> And Intensity anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T18:42:27-07:00","id":1143936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1143935#post1143935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity does not increase speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use a Vitae it multiplies your Speed by dots in Celerity plus one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T22:38:26-07:00","id":1143978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1143936#post1143936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you use a Vitae it multiplies your speed by dots in Celerity plus one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know. So they would have their speed multiplied by celerity +1 from the beginning and for all the duration of the devotion effect? It' s not the normal way crlerity works. Sounds weird to me... cool but weird <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And what they means with &quot;intensity&quot;?<br /> <br /> EDIT: book states Persistent effect only so that speed multiplier shouldn't be applied","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-26-2017, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T02:41:45-07:00","id":1144004,"title":"","content":"Honestly this is terrifying, just imagine rats flooding through the toilets, the bathtub, the air ducts, hell even smashing down the friggin wall and bursting through the floor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T02:58:05-07:00","id":1144010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144004#post1144004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly this is terrifying, just imagine rats flooding through the toilets, the bathtub, the air ducts, hell even smashing down the friggin wall and bursting through the floor</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree... what I'm saying is that it's something that we can apparently have with animalism 3, don't we?<br /> <br /> 10 vitae seems too much if I'm not missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T04:45:25-07:00","id":1144023,"title":"","content":"Have you read the whole effect of the Devotion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T05:07:33-07:00","id":1144028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144023#post1144023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the whole effect of the Devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes:<br /> - it give the swarm speed and intensity equal to &quot;permanent&quot; Celerity and Vigor value (still don't understand exactly how it is supposed to work, maybe you can clarify me this point),<br /> - It deal animalism lethal damage for the swarm (while normal swarm condition, taken from demon the descent, where it's stated that it is applied also to other different supernatural being able to control swarm - like, in this case, vampires with animalism 3 - can deal up to 4 bashing damage per turn, halves armor, give the distracted condition as well).<br /> - halves the speed of being beyond the swarm range<br /> - clean a crime scene.<br /> <br /> So that we have, in comparison with normal swarm condition, an upgrade from bashing to lethal, cleaning the crime scene and halves the speed. Yes ok, cool... but seriously: 10 vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:24:04-07:00","id":1144163,"title":"","content":"You do Animalism Lethal (at least 3) each turn to everything on the swarm radius, wich is as big as an small house. The Descent Swarm rules do 1 Bashing at its max radius and 1 additional Bashing every time they halve their radius to concentrate.<br /> <br /> Plus: Vermin Flood ignores any non-magical armor. Regular swarms allows for complete coverage Armor to be used, but offering only half its regular protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 09-26-2017, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:33:13-07:00","id":1144169,"title":"","content":"A small House is size 30, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:37:36-07:00","id":1144171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144163#post1144163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do Animalism Lethal (at least 3) each turn to everything on the swarm radius, wich is as big as an small house. The Descent Swarm rules do 1 Bashing at its max radius and 1 additional Bashing every time they halve their radius to concentrate.<br /> <br /> Plus: Vermin Flood ignores any non-magical armor. Regular swarms allows for complete coverage Armor to be used, but offering only half its regular protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I can remember right you &quot;divide&quot; the animalism lethal damage, as you wish, between any number of target into the swarm. Not full damage to everyone, that is similar to the descent swarm that can arrive to deal 4 bashing to a single target if you command your swarm to concentrate to only one target.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying its not better, just I'm not sure it is worth of 10 vitae while with 5 vitae you can hipotetically survive a nike bomb (Juggernaut), with 8 you can have all the stuff from force of nature and so on.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, what does &quot;with speed and intensity equal to vampire's celerity and vigor (permanent effect only)&quot; means?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually I was wrong, it is full the damage to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-26-2017, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T20:30:48-07:00","id":1144269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144171#post1144171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying its not better, just I'm not sure it is worth of 10 vitae while with 5 vitae you can hipotetically survive a nike bomb (Juggernaut), with 8 you can have all the stuff from force of nature and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ten Vitae for an explosive effect covering a fairly large &quot;small&quot; area for a scene seems about on-par with a more singular effect than Lord of the Land or Oubliette, either of which has a lower range of Vitae costs but comes with a fairly definite use condition besides &quot;smear blood everywhere.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the power doesn't simply generate the Swarm Tilt \u2014 individual animals don't all meet up together before arriving on the scene, nor do they necessarily glom into one big mass; a cat on its way to the alley full of blood is going to hit harder and stutter sideways from anyone trying to stop it. The pristine killbox is absolutely the main effect, but &quot;very little is going to actually stop the animals from arriving&quot; is worth remembering.<br /> <br /> Also also, Vermin Flood's prerequisites are intermediate competence in three common Disciplines. Juggernaut's Gait takes five dots in Resilience and is functionally useless without Blood Potency on par with an elder, while Force of Nature takes four dots in two different Disciplines, one of which is clan-specific, and gives you comparatively little that you don't already have from the prerequisites besides the ability to change them faster. Considering this is explicitly a more potent version of a power that costs two Vitae and can theoretically take as much as a full night to kick in, &quot;It happens pretty much immediately&quot; would justify a good deal of the extra cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T23:17:26-07:00","id":1144298,"title":"","content":"I'd simply interpret that as the animals gaining benefits of the Vampires Vigor and Celerity scores, persistent effects only so added strength and jumping capability from Vigor and added defense and dodge from Celerity, including limited defense against firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T00:39:26-07:00","id":1144307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144269#post1144269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ten Vitae for an explosive effect covering a fairly large &quot;small&quot; area for a scene seems about on-par with a more singular effect than Lord of the Land or Oubliette, either of which has a lower range of Vitae costs but comes with a fairly definite use condition besides &quot;smear blood everywhere.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the power doesn't simply generate the Swarm Tilt \u2014 individual animals don't all meet up together before arriving on the scene, nor do they necessarily glom into one big mass; a cat on its way to the alley full of blood is going to hit harder and stutter sideways from anyone trying to stop it. The pristine killbox is absolutely the main effect, but &quot;very little is going to actually stop the animals from arriving&quot; is worth remembering.<br /> <br /> Also also, Vermin Flood's prerequisites are intermediate competence in three common Disciplines. Juggernaut's Gait takes five dots in Resilience and is functionally useless without Blood Potency on par with an elder, while Force of Nature takes four dots in two different Disciplines, one of which is clan-specific, and gives you comparatively little that you don't already have from the prerequisites besides the ability to change them faster. Considering this is explicitly a more potent version of a power that costs two Vitae and can theoretically take as much as a full night to kick in, &quot;It happens pretty much immediately&quot; would justify a good deal of the extra cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Oubliette:</b></u><br /> 3 vitae for a small house, 9 for a big Mansion. Last Blood Potency Weeks<br /> It give you the capability to Use every Obfuscate power at no cost, reflexively and on any number of target at once and from any distance; It last Blood Potency weeks.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Force of Nature</u>:</b><br /> 8 vitae.<br /> - Move up to protean attributes at will (+4/5 to strength?)<br /> - Use any or all the transformation given by Protean 2, 3 and 4 reflexively and at no cost and all at the same time (You could have Horrid Talons, Wings, Barbed hands (+4/5 to grapple and lethal damages) all together and at no cost).<br /> It does not seems little things compared with the normal prerequisite powers O.o<br /> <br /> Now comparison between Animalism 3 and Vermin flood. I'm going to underline the different stuff given by each power:<br /> <br /> <b>Animalism 3:</b><br /> 2 Vitae. Last one night<br /> You have the Descent Swarm condition that gives you:<br /> - up to 4 Bashing per turn on a single target;<br /> - <u>Distracted condition to everyone (-2 on any rolls</u>);<br /> - Armor is not considered if not cover the whole body (like the cavalier one) and even in this case is halved;<br /> - Can't be attacked with nothing but explosion or other area attacks.<br /> - <u>as well as swarm you can also have: dogs (or even worst in a countryside)</u><br /> <br /> <b><u>Vermin flood:</u></b><br /> 10 vitae (8 more then animalism 3). Last one scene.<br /> - Animalism<u> lethal</u> to everyone<br /> - Ignore armor<br /> - <u>Clean crime scene</u><br /> - <u>halves speed</u><br /> - can't be attacked with nothing but area effects and fire.<br /> <br /> So that we have, in favor of vermin flood:<br /> <br /> - Lethal instead of bashing (which is good) and to everyone;<br /> - Clean crime scene (nice but...)<br /> - Halves Speed<br /> <br /> While we have in favor of animalism 3:<br /> <br /> - Bigger minions like dogs (possibly bear, Boars, which is really a plus) as well as the swarm.<br /> - Distracted condition with a fixed penalty of -2.<br /> - Last one night.<br /> <br /> Now: I'm not saying vermin flood sucks. Not at all. is really awesome and evocative. But 8 more vitae for just this effects it's not fair for me. But it's just my opinion and maybe I'm missing something in the equation. And anyway, we should not forget to take in account that, with Animalism 3, we can have dogs and bigger animals as well as swarm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1629_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1629\" data-vbnamecard=\"1629\">Possessed</a> : Adding Celerity to defense of a swarm, as far as the rules are written, is pretty much useless in my opinion, since the swarm can't be directly attacked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-27-2017, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T05:53:46-07:00","id":1144357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood#post1143918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Once activated, every animal of Size 2 or lower immediately swarms with the speed and intensity of the vampire\u2019s Celerity and <br /> Vigor (persistent effects only).*</div> </div> </div> </div>The animals need to get together before they can from a swarm, before that happens they do get utility out of having Celerity. And depending on the location and animals present this might prove to be a considerable edge. Naturally though YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T07:41:31-07:00","id":1144404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144307#post1144307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><b>Oubliette:</b></u><br /> 3 vitae for a small house, 9 for a big Mansion. Last Blood Potency Weeks<br /> It give you the capability to Use every Obfuscate power at no cost, reflexively and on any number of target at once and from any distance; It last Blood Potency weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Does not work until you spend a day asleep in the location.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><u>Force of Nature</u>:</b><br /> 8 vitae.<br /> - Move up to protean attributes at will (+4/5 to strength?) </div> </div> </div>This specifically works at no net gain in terms of Attribute dots \u2014 Boosting your Strength comes at the cost of your Dexterity or Stamina. It's notable as a tweak to Protean 3's &quot;assume the Physical Attributes of the animal you've consumed,&quot; but four dots of Strength for four points of Defense or four boxes of Health is a gambit, not a net boost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Use <b>any or all the transformation</b> given by Protean 2, 3 and 4 reflexively and at no cost and all at the same time (You could have Horrid Talons, Wings, Barbed hands (+4/5 to grapple and lethal damages) all together and at no cost).<br /> It does not seems little things compared with the normal prerequisite powers O.o </div> </div> </div>&quot;She can adopt additional modifications or shed existing ones as a reflexive action&quot; wouldn't have much point if you could just take the entire list plus anything you can come up with.<br /> <br /> Predatory Aspect normally gives you up to three benefits for one Vitae and Unnatural Aspect gives you one extra thing you can do for an extra Vitae. Being able to use and change the entire set of four abilities for free instantaneously is worth 8 Vitae without sticking the entire set of options on as well, because changing three Predatory Aspect abilities costs three Vitae and changing your Unnatural Aspect costs two more. Beast's Skin already lets you mess with your Attribute dots on a more fixed level. Completely changing your intermediate Protean loadout normally takes, at the very least, a full day and night of slumber.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can freely assume and incorporate and change any of the powers Protean 2-4 give you for free and mess with the stats of any form you have as well&quot; is a huge enough benefit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Animalism 3:</b><br /> 2 Vitae. Last one night<br /> <b>You have the Descent Swarm condition</b> that gives you: </div> </div> </div>You keep saying this, but it's wrong. You may wish to use the Tilt for expediency's sake, but the mechanics Vampire uses for swarms of animals in its relevant powers is not the Swarm Tilt. The Swarm Form Merit provides similar benefits to inflicting the Tilt, but &quot;apply the Swarm Tilt&quot; is not how any of the swarm-based powers do what they do.<br /> <br /> Animalism 3 lets you call a large number of animals to consume your blood and obey your command for a longer duration than Feral Whispers normally enables. That's the primary benefit it offers. Vermin Flood does one thing extremely well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While we have in favor of animalism 3:<br /> - Last one night. </div> </div> </div>Lasts [successes] nights. The Vitae stays potent for one night and disappears afterwards if not consumed, because it's primarily a vector for using Feral Whispers more effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-27-2017, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T07:51:29-07:00","id":1144408,"title":"","content":"In addition for Vermin Flood:<br /> - Can summon insects (which guaranty a swarm, while Summon the Hunt, depending on the circonstance, might not. You can even interpret that Summon the Hunt cannot create a swarm, since it's not mentioned anywhere how it work in the book, except perhaps adapting Swarm Form, but that's a stretch).<br /> - Swarm can't be destroyed until the end of the scene, as vermin keep coming to replenish the swarm.<br /> - Inflict Animalism damage in the whole area. Even if Summon the Hunt allow the use of swarm, you can only give one order. So you can leave an extended, low damage swarm covering the area, or concentrate a swarm on a single victim or small radius, easy to escape, area. You can't have a large area, high damage swarm (even if only bashing).<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd consider Vermin Flood to be the only way to summon a swarm, but I'm the first to consider Summon he Hunt to be a mess rulewise, and had the same issue as you with Vermin Flood. We can also discuss Feral Infection and Riot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T08:46:34-07:00","id":1144439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144408#post1144408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition for Vermin Flood:<br /> - Can summon insects (which guaranty a swarm, while Summon the Hunt, depending on the circonstance, might not. You can even interpret that Summon the Hunt cannot create a swarm, since it's not mentioned anywhere how it work in the book, except perhaps adapting Swarm Form, but that's a stretch).<br /> - Swarm can't be destroyed until the end of the scene, as vermin keep coming to replenish the swarm.<br /> - Inflict Animalism damage in the whole area. Even if Summon the Hunt allow the use of swarm, you can only give one order. So you can leave an extended, low damage swarm covering the area, or concentrate a swarm on a single victim or small radius, easy to escape, area. You can't have a large area, high damage swarm (even if only bashing).<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd consider Vermin Flood to be the only way to summon a swarm, but I'm the first to consider Summon he Hunt to be a mess rulewise, and had the same issue as you with Vermin Flood. We can also discuss Feral Infection and Riot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Summon the hunt can summon ANY animal in the range, even insects, since:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The vampire chooses when spilling the Vitae whether to summon <b>all predators and scavengers</b> </div> </div> </div>and insects are: animals for sure but also: predators (spider mantis...) or scavengers.<br /> <br /> All such animals from several city blocks/hundred meters actually forms a swarm. I really can't see any point why they shouldn't.<br /> Furthermore:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wherever she spills her blood \u2014 on the ground, over an object, or even splashing it on another person \u2014 the animals she calls will try to consume it </div> </div> </div>so that splashing blood on another person will lead the animals to automatically go on him to consume blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:00:44-07:00","id":1144446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144439#post1144439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summon the hunt can summon ANY animal in the range, even insects, since:</div> </div> </div> </div>Animalism, p 126<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Animalism powers affect predators and scavenging animals. In a city, the Kindred can call on feral cats and dogs, pigeons and crows, foxes, and more rats than anyone wants to think about. Rural vampires can summon bats, wolves, mountain lions, andeven bears \u2014 any animal that feasts on the flesh of another. </div> </div> </div>Animal is a loose term. Just check in Werewolf the Nature choirs, who distinguish Animals (Horses, Wolves, Bovines) from Fish, Birds, Reptiles and Insects <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .You have to thrust the exemple given instead of some ill defined word. Human are animals too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","user":"Nepher","date":". 09-27-2017, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:07:30-07:00","id":1144447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144446#post1144446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Animalism, p 126<br /> <br /> <br /> Animal is a loose term. Just check in Werewolf the Nature choirs, who distinguish Animals (Horses, Wolves, Bovines) from Fish, Birds, Reptiles and Insects <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .You have to thrust the exemple given instead of some ill defined word. Human are animals too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I got your point, but insects or not it shouldn't change the situation since, by rule, even animals of size 1 or 2 (cats, pigeons, crows, birds in general, rats, snakes etc.) are considered as Swarm when in big quantity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes, humans are animals but covered by domination because their complexity. Non the less animalism 4 acts also on them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-27-2017, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:18:36-07:00","id":1144453,"title":"","content":"Agreed, even if by RAW, there's no swarm mechanics in VtR, I'd allow it. But there's circumstances that forbid it (especially indoor). Vermin Flood circumvent that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:23:09-07:00","id":1144454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144453#post1144453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, even if by RAW, there's no swarm mechanics in VtR, I'd allow it. But there's circumstances that forbid it (especially indoor). Vermin Flood circumvent that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point actually. Well even if a flock of birds crashing the windows to get inside would be so cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:26:58-07:00","id":1144456,"title":"","content":"Actually, that's the point of Vermin Flood. These are birds with Vigor 2+ !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T09:30:02-07:00","id":1144459,"title":"","content":"I can fairly understand Vigor but still missing celerity (persistent) effect how it is involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T10:02:04-07:00","id":1144470,"title":"","content":"I thought Vermin Flood implied the persistent effects of vigor, and that the swarm moved as if they had activated the celerity speed effect.<br /> <br /> On the issue of Summon the Hunt, I don't think it works in swarms, especially because there is no swarm tilt in Vampire the Requiem. I've only ever seen it summon a pack of dogs and some birds, which did not constitute a swarm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T10:07:16-07:00","id":1144473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144470#post1144470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Vermin Flood implied the persistent effects of vigor, and that the swarm moved as if they had activated the celerity speed effect.<br /> <br /> On the issue of Summon the Hunt, I don't think it works in swarms, especially because there is no swarm tilt in Vampire the Requiem. I've only ever seen it summon a pack of dogs and some birds, which did not constitute a swarm.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the celerity matter, so why to specify: only persistent effect.<br /> <br /> About swarm: so, if as you said, animalism come back to be the more useless discipline in vampire. But this a part, why, if the text states: every animals in range, you should not allow swarm? Do you want to consider an hundred of birds, rats and whatever, one by one? I think swarm tilt is the best fitting thing and in Descent manual is specified that it's also valuable to other supernatural creatures then demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 09-27-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T10:34:33-07:00","id":1144484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144473#post1144473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About swarm: so, if as you said, animalism come back to be the more useless discipline in vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It lets you mess with minions without layering Conditions like Dominate and Majesty do and lets you establish a territory in which you are functionally untouchable by vampires. That's a pretty solid deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But this a part, why, if the text states: every animals in range, you should not allow swarm? </div> </div> </div>If you're calling a bunch of animals within a few blocks to eat your blood, you're not getting a swarm unless you're dealing with an outright infestation; and again, Summon the Hunt's primary use is in calling a number of animals to a set location and setting them to a particular task over a long period of time, not calling down a swarm of vermin on a painted target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T10:37:14-07:00","id":1144485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144473#post1144473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About swarm: so, if as you said, animalism come back to be the more useless discipline in vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why. Summoning a pack of stray dogs is far more potent than summoning a swarm. IMHO, Animalism is the most over powered combat discipline, especially because of level 3 &amp; 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T10:54:30-07:00","id":1144489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144485#post1144485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why. Summoning a pack of stray dogs is far more potent than summoning a swarm. IMHO, Animalism is the most over powered combat discipline, especially because of level 3 &amp; 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, why this discrimination through birds and rats? XD<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144484#post1144484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It lets you mess with minions without layering Conditions like Dominate and Majesty do and lets you establish a territory in which you are functionally untouchable by vampires. That's a pretty solid deal.<br /> <br /> If you're calling a bunch of animals within a few blocks to eat your blood, you're not getting a swarm unless you're dealing with an outright infestation; and again, Summon the Hunt's primary use is in calling a number of animals to a set location and setting them to a particular task over a long period of time, not calling down a swarm of vermin on a painted target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and a valid command, citated also in the book in aninalism 1, is: Attack. Furthermore the specification of the possibility to splash the blood directly on a target, what other meaning could have if not to let him beeing attacked without a direct command, in the attempt of consume blood by the animals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T10:59:06-07:00","id":1144491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144473#post1144473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About the celerity matter, so why to specify: only persistent effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says persistent effect only after vigor, so I assumed it meant that the swarm couldn't give themselves more damage with the effects of vigor. I don't see an issue with letting the celerity active effect work for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About swarm: so, if as you said, animalism come back to be the more useless discipline in vampire. But this a part, why, if the text states: every animals in range, you should not allow swarm? Do you want to consider an hundred of birds, rats and whatever, one by one? I think swarm tilt is the best fitting thing and in Descent manual is specified that it's also valuable to other supernatural creatures then demons. </div> </div> </div>Summon the Hunt doesn't summon that many animals. I don't believe hundreds of birds will be within a couple blocks of a city, and Vermin Flood is described as biblical in proportions. That's like summoning a plague of locusts, and stuff like that. Summon the Hunt is implied by the Vermin Flood devotion to be less of a masquerade break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T11:05:07-07:00","id":1144493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144491#post1144491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says persistent effect only after vigor, so I assumed it meant that the swarm couldn't give themselves more damage with the effects of vigor. I don't see an issue with letting the celerity active effect work for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Summon the Hunt doesn't summon that many animals. I don't believe hundreds of birds will be within a couple blocks of a city, and Vermin Flood is described as biblical in proportions. That's like summoning a plague of locusts, and stuff like that. Summon the Hunt is implied by the Vermin Flood devotion to be less of a masquerade break.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, lets add birds+rats+ cats (+ dogs)... and it's not rare to see flock of bird in the city sky. Furthermore the swarm tilt from descent talk about 8 yard range of animals of size 1 or 2 that it's less then 100 bird. I actually think that 100 is also a low number for this power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T11:22:07-07:00","id":1144498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144493#post1144493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, lets add birds+rats+ cats (+ dogs)... and it's not rare to see flock of bird in the city sky. Furthermore the swarm tilt from descent talk about 8 yard range of animals of size 1 or 2 that it's less then 100 bird. I actually think that 100 is also a low number for this power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Summon the Hunt also has a area limitation. You can only get an amount of blocks equal to your successes in a city, and in a rural area you get 90 meters for every success. This area limitation does limit the amount of animals you can summon.<br /> <br /> Vermin Flood, on the other hand, has no size limitations. From what I read, that means you're getting every cat, rat, bird, and insect in the city converging on your location. That sounds a lot more dangerous, and with vigor and celerity it becomes even scarier. Though you are right, the passive effects of celerity don't really help in this case. I think I'd personally just let the animals use the celerity power that increases speed in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T11:26:38-07:00","id":1144499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144489#post1144489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and a valid command, citated also in the book in aninalism 1, is: Attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Rats have individual stats, as do birds. You're not sending a bunch of normal rats after somebody hoping to do significant harm to them unless they're especially vulnerable \u2014 you send a bunch of small animals after somebody to make things difficult for them and wear them down, which is generally better accomplished with small groups or singular attackers if your goal is real damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore the specification of the possibility to splash the blood directly on a target, what other meaning could have if not to let him beeing attacked without a direct command, in the attempt of consume blood by the animals? </div> </div> </div>&quot;What other meaning could this have?&quot; is kind of a silly thing to ask when you have the entire breadth of possible commands to apply to the animals that arrive and you can command them to attack a person without getting the blood <i>on</i> that target \u2014 &quot;keep other people away from this person&quot; is valid, as is &quot;follow this person, then come back to me,&quot; as are more involved effects like giving an animal an object painted to attract a different kind of animal and sending them to leave the object in a particular place to prompt a particular order on a delay.<br /> <br /> The primary use of Summon the Hunt is to expand the ways in which you can use Feral Whispers. Inflicting the Distracted Condition on people caught amidst a bunch of small animals is an option, and in fact that is the main consistent effect of the Swarm Environmental Tilt as represented in the mechanics of gamelines whose 2e books do not reproduce the entire Tilt as a specific printed game mechanic, but nothing about Vampire's mechanics for swarms necessitates messing around with diameter and condensing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-27-2017, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T11:32:25-07:00","id":1144502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144499#post1144499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. Rats have individual stats, as do birds.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;What other meaning could this have?&amp;quot; is kind of a silly thing to ask when you have the entire breadth of possible commands to apply to the animals that arrive and you can command them to attack a person without getting the blood <i>on</i> that target \u2014 &amp;quot;keep other people away from this person&amp;quot; is valid, as is &amp;quot;follow this person, then come back to me,&amp;quot; as are more involved effects like giving an animal an object painted to attract a different kind of animal and sending them to leave the object in a particular place to prompt a particular order on a delay.<br /> <br /> The primary use of Summon the Hunt is to expand the ways in which you can use Feral Whispers. Inflicting the Distracted Condition on people caught amidst a bunch of small animals is an option, and in fact that is the main consistent effect of the Swarm Environmental Tilt as represented in the mechanics of gamelines whose 2e books do not reproduce the entire Tilt as a specific printed game mechanic, but nothing about Vampire's mechanics for swarms necessitates messing around with diameter and condensing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I disagree here, spilling blood on a target lead the animals to feed it from its body that is nothing less then an attack. The meaning is that, if not spilled directly on a person, you have to wait for them to feed it then another turn to command them to do something; which is not so much valuable in a fight. Otherwise spilling on a person lead them to attack him wothout a specific command (read: a turn less).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T11:45:34-07:00","id":1144504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144502#post1144502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I disagree here, spilling blood on a target lead the animals to feed it from its body that is nothing less then an attack. The meaning is that, if not spilled directly on a person, you have to wait for them to feed it then another turn to command them to do something; which is not so much valuable in a fight. Otherwise spilling on a person lead them to attack him wothout a specific command (read: a turn less).</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, I consider Summon the Hunt to be messy rule wise, having to make several call in game to be usable. My personal interpretation of this point is that the command is imprinted in the blood (the vampire don't need to be there for the animal to consume the blood and get the command. The blood may be tasted during all the night, and the animals gain the same order), so you don't lose a turn giving a command (or even have to wait for the animals to arrive).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T11:46:44-07:00","id":1144505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143918-vermin-flood?p=1144502#post1144502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I disagree here, spilling blood on a target lead the animals to feed it from its body that is nothing less then an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It leads to the animals trying to consume the blood that is on them. That's surface wounds at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The meaning is that, if not spilled directly on a person, you have to wait for them to feed it then another turn to command them to do something; which is not so much valuable in a fight. </div> </div> </div>If you have a bunch of animals close by enough to be thinking about using them in a fight, the only reason you have to use Summon the Hunt is so you can see them.<br /> <br /> Looking at Disciplines solely in terms of what is most useful in turn-based combat is inherently going to skew your priorities when we're talking about a game where the player characters are immortals who have to dedicate resources to healing and can maintain proxies in a number of different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}